      "lineNbr": 423,
      "author": {
        "id": 1514900
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-10T14:51:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes - this is more of an artifact of how the current apex() rule is generating the staging directory and canned fs config in Bazel. Within the Starlark rule, we are able to predetermine the staging dir layout and fs config content using static information like module name, type, and hardcoded paths, but the checksum of a dep is dynamic and thus isn\u0027t available. We\u0027ll need to move the apex() rule to use a host tool instead.\n\nThat\u0027s why moving these commands that control paths to a host tool on the Soong side will make it simpler to transition to Bazel.",
      "parentUuid": "fd4c37fd_68c87461",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 423,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 423,
        "endChar": 91
      },
